 The let-go issue draft now carries an llvm section built from this one: the shared seam with nothing added, the packaging cost (clang and lld on the machine, the host runtime in C, the compile time against git-issue:d2b7f41's plan), the rt/llvm fork of rt/wasm named as deliberate, and the benchmark lines with the interop caveat kept beside them. The packaging order stays as git-issue:c2838dd has it, with the llvm lowering last.
 
